{"duration_api_ms":22195,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"afef46fb-2e2a-4c59-b5d1-cc0529a56af6","total_cost_usd":0.12583499999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11621,"cache_read_input_tokens":120550,"output_tokens":2179,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":674},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11621},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":2179,"cacheReadInputTokens":120550,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11621,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.12583499999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":674,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I fixed `Hijack()` so websocket libraries can take over the connection again; the full test suite passes, but I couldn't commit because git has no author name or email set here.\n\n**The problem:** `responseWriter.Hijack()` in `response_writer.go` (changed in #4295) refused to hijack as soon as `Written()` was true. That includes the point where only the headers have been sent and no body has been written yet. Some websocket libraries, such as `github.com/coder/websocket`, send the `101 Switching Protocols` headers first and then hijack, so they always failed with `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n\n**The fix:** Hijacking is now refused only once body data has been written. It's still allowed before anything is written and after only the headers have been sent. The protection #4295 added against hijacking after a body write is unchanged.\n\n**Tests:** I added two cases to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite` in `response_writer_test.go`: hijacking after `WriteHeaderNow()` with status 101, and hijacking after `Flush()`. Both expect success. `gofmt` reports nothing.\n\nThe changes are in the working tree, uncommitted. If you set `user.name` and `user.email` (or tell me what to use), I'll commit with the message `fix(response): refine hijack behavior for response lifecycle`.","ttft_ms":4136,"type":"result","duration_ms":25661,"uuid":"64530f86-15c9-4354-9329-f25731d08183","ttft_stream_ms":1351,"time_to_request_ms":95,"first_content_frame_ms":1351,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
